<title>USA: EDS gets $700-$900 mln EBS contract.</title>
<headline>EDS gets $700-$900 mln EBS contract.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electronic Data Systems Corp said it expects revenues of between $700 million and $900 million from a new contract with EBS, a provider of electronic broking services for interbank spot foreign exchange.</p>
<p>Electronic Data said it was selected by EBS to manage its global dealing network and provide related technical-support services.</p>
<p>EBS is owned by subsidiaries of 14 financial services companies and MINEX Corp of Japan.</p>
</text>
